# instances.list — the linked / WordPress-integrated ODR instances on this server, one per line.
#
# Copy this to  app/config/instances.list  (which is gitignored — it's per-server) and list each
# instance: its ROOT directory (the dir that contains app/config, NOT the app dir), then its cache
# key — the memcached_key_prefix its cache entries are stored under.  Keys must be unique, and may
# only contain letters, digits and _.
#
# Used by  app/console-all  to fan a single console command out across every site:
#     sudo php app/console-all cache:clear --env=prod
# Before clearing each site's cache, that brings the site's parameters.yml in line with this list:
#     memcached_key_prefix            the site's key
#     session_memcached_prefix        the site's key + "_sess"
#     related_memcached_key_prefixes  the keys of the other sites listed here that use the same
#                                     database
# so this list must name every site on the server that shares a database with another.
# Check without changing anything:  php app/console-all --check-params
#
# Also used by  setup_virtualhost.sh --all  (which only needs the root).
#
# Blank lines and everything after a '#' are ignored.  A line with only a root still works, but
# that site's parameters.yml isn't checked.
#
# Example:
# /home/odr/data-publisher     odr_master
# /home/rruff/data-publisher   odr_rruff
# /home/amcsd/data-publisher   odr_amcsd
